+# Checklist: create-and-scene
+
+Merged verification plan; checks are planned, not recorded as passed. IDs retain all original lead (L) and implementor (I) citations; combined rows keep both. X rows cover definition gaps found during crosscheck. Spec references abbreviate files under `specs/`; project instructions refer to the supplied repository instructions. Overlapping source rows are split where independent behaviors need different checks.
+
+The lead resolved timing, scaling, and styling discrepancies in the external `acceptance-assumptions.md` record: entry may start when layout motion finishes; scale changes with viewport/mode/canvas but not step; geometry/motion and caller styles are allowed while kit visual defaults are forbidden. Existing rulings also settle hook aliases, attribution URL, unknown-route fallback, and non-empty-project confirmation scope. No user decision is pending. Checks below apply those rulings within the approved definition.
+
+Checks use automated tests, commands, or file inspection. Procedural skill requirements are checked in the distributed instructions/templates rather than by running an agent through the workflow. Screenshot files may be inspected after scripted capture; advisory diagnostics alone are not proof of visual quality. Only the test plan's named integration and end-to-end cases are planned. This merge does not assert implementation or verification completion.
+
